What:		/proc/game_opt/render_thread_info
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read/write interface for bounded render-thread waker telemetry.
		Writing up to two decimal thread IDs enables accounting for wakeups
		to those render threads by threads in the same process.  Writing an
		empty string or zero disables accounting.  Accounting is disabled
		at boot, uses a non-blocking scheduler hot-path lock, and stores at
		most 256 waker records.  Reads return the ten most active wakers per
		render thread as:

		<tid>;<comm>;<render_tid>;<total_wakes>;<wakes_since_read>

		Reading resets only the final per-read wake counter.

What:		/proc/game_opt/rt_num
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only diagnostic summary of the configured render threads and
		the bounded waker-record pool.  The first line is "rt_num <count>".
